    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref> entity bound to the <computeroutput>clinics</computeroutput> table; the organisation root for clinic cases. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Like the other service types, this is a thin value type that fixes the table name for the inherited Service/Entity SQL builders. CRUD/search and staff management are inherited. Instances are built from one of the <ref refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2_1_1Types" kindref="compound">api::v2::Types</ref> data wrappers, which <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> stores as an <ref refid="entity_8hpp_1aa7ee46136fb273d4151dc647393adcdd" kindref="member">EntityType</ref> variant. The type satisfies api::v2::Service_t and is selected through the <computeroutput>clinics</computeroutput> entries of the services and staff route registries. In addition, <computeroutput>clinics</computeroutput> is the organisation referenced by <ref refid="classCase_1a7845d0ed5ca20c2a1de1adeadae345ae" kindref="member">Case::ORGNAME</ref>: every <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref> permission query joins this table to recover the owning clinic&apos;s owner/admin/staff columns through the case&apos;s clinic_id. Ownership: the wrapper is copied into the base and is const thereafter; no other resources are owned. No mutable state or locking of its own. Copy and move are deleted by <ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref>: construct a fresh instance per operation. <simplesect kind="note"><para>No default constructor: <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref> needs a data wrapper to build statements from. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref>, <ref refid="classEntity" kindref="compound">Entity</ref>, <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref>, <ref refid="classServiceController" kindref="compound">ServiceController</ref>, <ref refid="classStaffController" kindref="compound">StaffController</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
